The first run exposed a performance bug in my greedy attack: for the first letter there is only one possible insertion triple, but the sampler was trying to collect 64 distinct triples. I stopped the run, fixed that finite-space case, and am also replacing a cubic projection scan with cached occurrence positions; the gate definitions and sample counts remain unchanged.
